    [Refactor] Split AscendStore layerwise pool worker and scheduler (#20140)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Follow up on #19885 by moving the remaining layerwise AscendStore worker
    and scheduler behavior into `LayerwiseKVPoolWorker` and
    `LayerwiseKVPoolScheduler`. The connector selects these subclasses
    through explicit factories, while the base classes retain ordinary pool
    behavior.
    
    This also consolidates backend-specific layerwise key binding and
    validation in the Mooncake and Memcache backend classes, removes
    obsolete protocol wrappers, and updates affected imports and unit-test
    fixtures. During the rebase onto current `main`, the upstream PP/GVA
    byte-offset handling was preserved in the extracted worker.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No expected user-facing behavior change. This is an internal ownership
    and inheritance refactor. Internal direct constructors that previously
    depended on `__new__` dispatch now use the connector factories.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `bash format.sh ci` passed across all files, including Markdown.
    - `git diff --check` passed.
    - Focused mypy 1.11.1 checks passed for all 25 AscendStore source files
    with Python targets 3.10, 3.11 and 3.12 (`--follow-imports skip
    --check-untyped-defs --ignore-missing-imports`). External vLLM/torch
    dependencies are unavailable locally; complete CI type checking remains
    required.
    - Added `TestDSparkPrefixRegistration` in
    `tests/ut/distributed/ascend_store/test_pool_worker.py` to cover draft
    registration on the final pipeline stage and skipping earlier stages.
    The test file passes a separate focused mypy check.
    - An isolated execution of the actual registration methods passed for
    the base no-op, disabled prefix reuse, non-final pipeline stage and
    final-stage draft registration. This uses dependency stubs and does not
    establish NPU correctness.
    - Attempted focused worker, scheduler and connector tests; collection is
    blocked locally by missing upstream vLLM modules and unbuilt Ascend
    package metadata. Full CPU UT and NPU validation remain for CI.
    
    CPU CI follow-up (`45b0adca9`): both upstream-main and v0.32.0 jobs
    exposed the same 985 fixture setup errors (attention-gate mocks still
    targeted the base worker module) and 30 PP regressions using methods
    moved to the layerwise subclass. Updated the scoped mocks and both PP
    regression files to use the new module/class locations; assertions and
    test cases are retained. `bash format.sh ci`, `git diff --check`, and
    separate focused mypy checks for the two PP files passed. Local pytest
    cannot load the shared fixture because torch is not installed; rerun CPU
    CI is required.
    
    Further CPU CI follow-up (`abedb4781`): the fixture setup errors and PP
    regressions are resolved; the previous main/release runs passed
    13,044/13,034 tests and exposed the same remaining 29 failures in
    layerwise test fixtures. Connector tests now mock the worker factory,
    GVA task tests construct the layerwise worker, and GLM final-save tests
    bind methods from the extracted class. `bash format.sh ci`, `git diff
    --check` and focused mypy checks for all three affected test files
    passed. Isolated execution of the two real GLM final-save tests against
    the real extracted save methods passed (dependency stubs, not full
    integration). Full CPU/NPU CI remains required because local torch/vLLM
    dependencies are unavailable.
    
    Latest CI evidence for `abedb4781`:
    
    - [Full E2E
    workflow](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40701155435)
    passed: 33 successful checks, 5 skipped, no pending or failed checks.
    Merge-conflict check and DCO also passed.
    - [Pre-commit, including full CI
    mypy](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40701155435/job/122861013784)
    passed.
    - CPU UT passed against both [verified upstream
    main](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40701155435/job/122863884631)
    and
    [v0.32.0](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40701155435/job/122863884591).
    - Selected NPU checks and upstream E2E passed. The [A2 part 3/7
    retry](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40701155435/job/122912284988)
    passed after a transient ModelScope HTTP 503 download failure. The [A5
    four-card
    retry](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40701155435/job/122964605861)
    passed after the internal Git CDN checkout connectivity failure. Each
    affected task was retried once; no test assertions were disabled to
    handle these infrastructure failures.
    
    Existing AscendStore tests and fixtures were updated for the class and
    import moves. CI fixes correct layerwise type annotations, declare
    scheduler initialization hooks and move DSpark draft-cache registration
    into the layerwise worker without changing the registration point.
    
    ---
    
    ### Checklist
    
    #### Testing
    
    - [x] **Boundary / edge-case coverage**: Existing lookup, PP, DCP, and
    layerwise test coverage was retained and adjusted for the new class
    locations.
    - [ ] **Regression test**: This PR is a refactor rather than a targeted
    bug fix.
    - [x] **Error / failure path coverage**: Existing backend validation and
    transfer failure tests were retained.
    - [x] **Meaningful & reliable tests**: Updated tests continue to assert
    the existing behavior, pending execution in a matching CI environment.
    - [ ] **Performance impact**: No performance claim is made; NPU
    profiling remains pending.
    
